	"profile": "supermicro-sys-112b-fwt",
	"name": "Supermicro SYS-112B-FWT",
	"chassis": "CSE-515B-R000WNP2",
	"board": "X14SBW-TF",
	"units": "mm",
	"frame": "As the -WR profile: origin at the bottom centre of the FRONT face, +x right looking at the front, +y up, +z out of the front; the chassis runs from z = 0 back to z = -depth. This is a FRONT-I/O chassis: the PSUs, LAN1/LAN2, the BMC port, COM, USB, VGA and all three expansion-slot openings are on the front face; the rear is a blank vented panel with the service tag.",
	"sources": {
		"spec": "supermicro.com SYS-112B-FWT: 1U, 436.88 x 44.5 x 429.3 mm, 2 internal fixed 2.5in NVMe/SATA bays, 2 x M.2 PCIe 5.0 x2 (2280/22110), 2 x FHFL + 1 x LP PCIe x16, up to 6 x 4 cm fans, 2 x 800 W 1+1 redundant PSU",
		"qrg": "MNL-2726-QRG-100 (system) front photo: left to right AC Power Supply 2, AC Power Supply 1, power button with status LED above COM1, dedicated IPMI LAN above USB, LAN1, LAN2, VGA, slot 3 (LP) above the LAN/VGA block, slots 1 (upper) and 2 (lower) FHFL at the right. MNL-2675-QRG-110 (board): DIMMs in two banks of four flanking the socket, FAN1-FAN6 headers on the edge away from the I/O, JM2_1/JM2_2 on the left edge, rear I/O order COM1, BMC_LAN, USB0/1, LAN1, LAN2, VGA, UID",
		"inventory": "GB process cluster node1, 2026-10-04: dmidecode slots M.2-C1 (bus 34, nvme1) and M.2-C2 (bus 35, nvme0) in use; RSC-W-66G5 SLOT1 x16 in use (Mellanox ConnectX-6 Lx, 2 x SFP28, bus 84), RSC-W-66G5 SLOT2 x16 free, RSC-WR-6G5-UP SLOT1 x16 LP free; DIMMA1/C1/E1/G1 32 GB each; IPMI PS1/PS2 Status present on all four nodes; FAN1-FAN6 all reporting; onboard Intel X550 LAN1/LAN2 (bus 36)",
		"unverified": "NOT MEASURED. Front-face x positions are scaled from the QRG front photo (about 1.45 px/mm); every depth (z) is inferred: the board's I/O edge at the front, fans behind the board, the two internal 2.5in bays at the rear right. Which riser slot is the UPPER opening (chassis slot 1 vs 2) is assumed SLOT1 = upper. M.2 positions are from the board diagram. Fan order left to right is assumed FAN1..FAN6 following the headers. Nobody is on site; refine from a photo with the lid off when GB sends one."
	},
